{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-1",
      "transcript": "Earth had nuclear reactors about two billion years ago. Nobody built them.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-1.wav",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 5.15,
      "beatIndex": 0,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.1",
      "samples": 123600,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-2",
      "transcript": "At Oklo, in what is now Gabon, uranium-rich rock sustained nuclear chain reactions.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-2.wav",
      "start": 5.533333333333333,
      "duration": 6.325,
      "beatIndex": 1,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.2",
      "samples": 151800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-3",
      "transcript": "Scientists found the clues in 1972: missing uranium-235, and the distinctive products of fission.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-3.wav",
      "start": 12.066666666666666,
      "duration": 8.45,
      "beatIndex": 2,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.3",
      "samples": 202800,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-4",
      "transcript": "But radioactive rock alone is not a reactor. One splitting nucleus must release neutrons that can split more nuclei, keeping a chain going.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-4.wav",
      "start": 20.733333333333334,
      "duration": 9.8,
      "beatIndex": 3,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.4",
      "samples": 235200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-5",
      "transcript": "Back then, natural uranium contained more uranium-235, because that isotope decays faster than uranium-238.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-5.wav",
      "start": 30.733333333333334,
      "duration": 10.8,
      "beatIndex": 4,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.5",
      "samples": 259200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Geology concentrated the uranium. The deposit had to retain enough neutrons, with few impurities that would absorb them.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-6.wav",
      "start": 41.733333333333334,
      "duration": 8.55,
      "beatIndex": 5,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.6",
      "samples": 205200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-7",
      "transcript": "Groundwater supplied another crucial ingredient.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-7.wav",
      "start": 50.666666666666664,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "beatIndex": 6,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.7",
      "samples": 79200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-8",
      "transcript": "Collisions with hydrogen in the water slowed the neutrons, making further uranium-235 fissions more likely. Enough kept the chain alive.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-8.wav",
      "start": 54.166666666666664,
      "duration": 10.6,
      "beatIndex": 7,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.8",
      "samples": 254400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-9",
      "transcript": "In one studied reaction zone, xenon isotope evidence points to repeated starts and stops.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-9.wav",
      "start": 64.96666666666667,
      "duration": 6.475,
      "beatIndex": 8,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.9",
      "samples": 155400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-10",
      "transcript": "Researchers infer that heating drove moderating water away, stopping the chain. Cooling let water return, and fission restart.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-10.wav",
      "start": 71.83333333333333,
      "duration": 8.925,
      "beatIndex": 9,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.10",
      "samples": 214200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-11",
      "transcript": "That cycle is reconstructed from traces in the rock, not an ancient clock anyone watched.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-11.wav",
      "start": 80.96666666666667,
      "duration": 6.1,
      "beatIndex": 10,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.11",
      "samples": 146400,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    },
    {
      "id": "oklo-cue-12",
      "transcript": "No machinery. No electricity. Just heat from nuclear fission, sustained by fuel, water, and geology, long before humans existed.",
      "file": "audio/oklo/narration/cue-12.wav",
      "start": 87.26666666666667,
      "duration": 9.925,
      "beatIndex": 11,
      "sourceScriptSegmentId": "oklo.asset.natural-reactors.script.12",
      "samples": 238200,
      "sampleRate": 24000
    }
  ],
